# Markdown formatting

Follow the [Consensys Markdown formatting guide](https://docs-template.consensys.com/contribute/format-markdown)
for full details. The rules below cover the most common conventions.

## Line length and sentence breaks

- When writing prose, wrap at about 100 characters. Start each sentence on its own line.

## Links

- Use relative file paths for links between documentation pages (for example,
  `./concepts/architecture.md` or `../reference/cli-options.md`).
- Use descriptive link text. Do not use "click here" or bare URLs.
- Docusaurus is configured with `onBrokenLinks: 'throw'` and `onBrokenMarkdownLinks: 'throw'`.
  Broken internal links will fail the build.

## Code blocks

- Always specify the language on fenced code blocks (` ```javascript `, ` ```bash `, etc.).
- Indent code with two spaces, not four.
- Write code samples that can be copied, pasted, and run as-is. Do not include shell prompts
  (for example, `user@host $`) or trailing comments that break execution.
- Use angle-bracket placeholders for values the reader must supply
  (for example, `<YOUR_NODE_URL>`).

## Tabs

- Use Docusaurus `<Tabs>` and `<TabItem>` components to display parallel content such as
  command-line syntax or configuration in different formats (for example, TOML vs command-line).
- Import `Tabs` and `TabItem` from `@theme/Tabs` and `@theme/TabItem` at the top of the file.

## Admonitions

- Use Docusaurus admonitions: `:::note`, `:::tip`, `:::caution`, `:::info`, `:::danger`.
- Add a custom title on the same line only when it helps scanning (for example,
  `:::caution important`).
- Do not nest admonitions.

## Tables

- Align table columns in the source Markdown for readability.
- Use a tool like [Markdown Table Formatter](https://markdowntable.com/) if needed.

## Frontmatter

- Required: `description` (one sentence for SEO and previews).
- Recommended: `keywords` (array).
- `sidebar_label`: optional. Use sparingly; only when the default sidebar text (usually from the
  page title) would be too long or wordy for the navigation. Omit when the default is fine.
- If the frontmatter contains a `title` field, do not add a separate top-level `# Heading` to
  avoid a duplicate H1.

## File and folder names

- Use lowercase letters and dashes only (for example, `configure-logging.md`, not
  `configureLogging.md`).

## Prettier

A Husky pre-commit hook runs Prettier on staged Markdown, MDX, JavaScript, and JSON.
CI checks documentation Markdown with `npm run format:docs:check`.

Prettier preserves existing line breaks in Markdown and MDX. It can break a Markdown
list nested in HTML or JSX. Wrap that block so Prettier leaves it alone. Put both
comments at the start of the line:

- In `.md` files, use `<!-- prettier-ignore-start -->` and `<!-- prettier-ignore-end -->`.
- In `.mdx` files, use `{/* prettier-ignore-start */}` and `{/* prettier-ignore-end */}`.

Use the form that matches the file type. HTML comments fail MDX compilation, and
Prettier does not recognize JSX comments in Markdown.
